drm/amd/display: enable the second tile on Apple 27" 5K iMac internal panels (lean)

The 27" 5K iMac internal panel (iMac15,1 / 17,1 / 18,3 / 19,1 / 20,x /
iMacPro1,1) is a 2x1 tiled display driven over two links: an eDP root tile
and a DP second tile. Mac firmware only brings the second link up for macOS
and Windows; on Linux it stays powered down (HPD low, AUX dead), so amdgpu
sees a single 2560x2880 tile and the panel scales it, or falls back to the
3840x2160 timing.

Per the Windows driver's EnableSecondaryTileIfRequired path, writing 1 to
the vendor DPCD register 0x4F1 on the eDP root wakes the second tile's link.
This patch adds a panel quirk (apply_edid_quirks, keyed on the Apple panel
IDs) that:

  * wires the eDP root and its DP sibling as a tile pair (link->tiled_peer),
  * pulses the root latch (0x4F1) before probing / link-training the slave,
    polls the slave's DPCD until AUX answers, and treats it as connected even
    with HPD low,
  * publishes the source-DPCD table revision the Boot Camp driver uses,
    re-pulses the latch at stream enable, and re-reads the root EDID once the
    slave exposes its tile block (the root's EDID flips to its tile identity),
  * prefers the tile-native mode on both connectors,
  * enables the per-frame CRTC reset on both tile streams, before the master
    pick, so the two tiles scan out in lockstep (multi_sync is otherwise left
    disabled in mainline); the panel TCON only latches dual-tile mode when the
    tiles are genlocked, and enabling the reset after the pick left the lock
    to chance (a stale flag from the previous commit).
  * puts the panel back the way the firmware expects it at reboot: the wake
    leaves the second tile latched on, and Apple's firmware then draws its
    boot logo skewed on the next warm boot (verified against a stock control).
    amdgpu_pci_shutdown() never disables the streams on the reboot path, so
    for a tiled panel it now runs drm_atomic_helper_shutdown() with a
    going-down flag set (wake paths and tiled re-detects become no-ops), the
    slave's stream-off clears 0x4F1 / 0x310 / 0x10A, and the root eDP panel
    is powered off and held for T12.

Both connectors then carry correct DisplayID tile metadata and the compositor
stitches them (Mutter today; KWin in progress). Tested on iMac18,3
(Radeon Pro 575 / POLARIS10 / DCE 11.2): native 5120x2880, both tiles HBR2x4,
sync_enabled=1, seamless under motion. Also builds against 7.1.x.

This is a lean rework of the community patch series (mcirsta/linux-imac-5k,
ported by taprobane99): all bring-up instrumentation/logging removed, the
dead plumbing that only fed it stripped, and the no-op refactor of
dc/core/dc.c dropped. 770 added lines vs 1631.

